From 212914fad6c8008b0294a8856cf95162677146d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:41:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): release rejected merge-queue PRs to repair
 workers [daveey]

Five whys: repair stalled because active_pr held an OPEN PR; the PR stayed open after queue rejection; the guard queried only GitHub lifecycle state; queue completion was not modeled; tests covered merged/closed but no rejected-open case. The earlier terminal-state fix therefore did not cover queue failures. Read the newest bb-land marker, require done=true plus rejected or exit=2, quote its reason once on the card, and resume repair rather than duplicate creation. Unknown/malformed/queued evidence still holds. Do not cache rejection across requeue. Proof: rejection regression failed before the change; 114 dispatch, park and review tests pass, including queued/latest-marker, malformed, merged, deduped reason and requeue controls.
